  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="386f7e63-5eaf-5baa-84f7-2ca1d510df95" activityNameId="8529f811-8996-5628-8e67-9aa54e27aa5b" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Sheet rolling, chromium steel</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Sheet rolling, chromium steel
This process is to be used only for high alloyed (chromium) steel. For many applications, the products of hot rolling are unsatisfactory, e.g., with respect to cross section, surface quality, dimensional accuracy, and general finish, so that cold rolling is necessary. Cold rolled products are mainly strips and sheets with high quality surface finish and precise metallurgical properties for use in high specification products. ;
UUID: 8f574699-0784-38ab-8f35-770310aaa795
Includes the process steps annealing (I) and pickling (I), cold rolling, annealing (II) and pickling (II), tempering, inspecting and finishing, packing coils or sheets, roll maintenance. Does not include the material beeing rolled.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Average technique for EU, for high-alloyed or chromium steel.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: Less than 2.5 million tonnes per year (Zeltner --&gt; 5%Stahl)
Sampling: Literature 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: The fact that no data were available about the percentage of companies represented by the study citated is considered in the uncertainties.
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_8f574699-0784-38ab-8f35-770310aaa795.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
